  "note": "虹台 (native:waterfog/terrace_stair, terrace, terrace_edge; 大会 A): the white stair up a narrow ridge from 葬剑亭, gorges either side and the mist coming up them; the round top of the peak paved with old white slabs, cracked and sunk, grass in the joints, worn smooth where feet go; the 擎天柱 in the middle with a cold censer before it, nine stone flag seats round the rim with bare poles and a rag or two of last year's flags, the 盟主's stone chair with leaves on its seat; west the rough lip over 虹谷, a cairn and a dead pine log, the mist rising and by day a faint rainbow in it. 水烟阁 across the gorge to the north-east. Deep valleys on three sides. Empty but on the day; no one lives here: old, weathered, not tidy.",
